&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is a US-headquartered, global leader in agent-first brokerage infrastructure&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;for stocks, ETFs, options, crypto, fixed income, 24/5 trading, and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Amongst our subsidiaries, Alpaca is a licensed financial services company, serving hundreds of financial institutions across 40 countries with our institutional-grade APIs. This includes broker-dealers, investment advisors, wealth managers, hedge funds, and crypto exchanges, totalling over 10 million brokerage accounts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our global team is a diverse group of experienced engineers, traders, and brokerage professionals who are working to achieve our mission of opening financial services to everyone on the planet. We&#39;re deeply committed to open-source contributions and fostering a vibrant community, continuously enhancing our award-winning, developer-friendly API and the robust infrastructure behind it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alpaca is proudly backed by $400 million in funding from top-tier global investors including Portage Ventures, Spark Capital, Tribe Capital, Social Leverage, Horizons Ventures, Opera Tech Ventures, SBI Group, Derayah Financial, Unbound, Peak XV, Elefund, and Y Combinator.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Team Members:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic team of 400+ globally distributed members who thrive working from our favorite places around the world, with teammates spanning the USA, Canada, Japan, Hungary, Nigeria, Brazil, the UK, and beyond!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We&#39;re searching for passionate individuals eager to contribute to Alpaca&#39;s rapid growth. If you align with our core values—Stay Curious, Have Empathy, and Be Accountable—and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;ak-renderer-extension  &quot; data-layout=&quot;default&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ak-renderer-extension-overflow-container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;css-k008qs&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and execute borrow and loan opportunities across various asset classes (equities, fixed income, ETFs) using both manual and automated trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage Python and SQL to streamline daily tasks, develop analytical tools, and automate data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product, Engineering, and Operations teams to optimize data pipelines, trading systems, operational efficiency and risk controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor outstanding loans, recalls, and rates to optimize risk and profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with borrowers, lenders, custodians, and firm client partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and perform operational tasks, product improvements, and automation tools for optimizing costs, revenue and workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and manage counterparty, credit, and market risk while staying informed of market developments and regulatory changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with existing and new securities lending vendors on product development solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to creating automated workflow solutions for securities lending trading and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Mathematics, Finance, Economics or a related quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-5 years of experience in a technical or trading role, ideally with some exposure to securities lending, short selling or related experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Python and SQL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, quantitative, and problem-solving abilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with core financial instruments (equities, fixed income, ETFs) and general market mechanics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent collaboration and communication skills to work across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High initiative and eagerness to learn about securities lending, product development, and advanced trading concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
